go2 context: stand aside for an explicit video_context_driver = "kms"

Both DRM contexts have the ident "kms", because udev_input.c keys keyboard
handling on it, so the setting could never select the generic one: the go2
context is first in the list and answers. An unrotated panel can use direct
page flips instead of an RGA copy of every frame. The default "" still
tries go2 first, so rotated consoles are unaffected.

--- a/gfx/drivers_context/drm_go2_ctx.c
+++ b/gfx/drivers_context/drm_go2_ctx.c
@@ -118,6 +118,16 @@
    if (!drm)
       return NULL;
 
+   /* Both contexts are called "kms" and this one is tried first, so an
+    * explicit "kms" reaches the generic context only if this one stands
+    * aside. It costs an RGA copy per frame that an unrotated panel does
+    * not need. */
+   if (string_is_equal(config_get_ptr()->arrays.video_context_driver, "kms"))
+   {
+      free(drm);
+      return NULL;
+   }
+
    drm->display       = go2_display_create();
 
    /* Auto-detect rotation from console_detect */
